{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_12",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_12_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_9",
      "quote": "We used meta-analysis to evaluate the pooled rate of SARS-CoV-2 reinfection in the included studies... we decided to use the logit transformation",
      "reason": "The text specifies the outcome (SARS-CoV-2 reinfection rate) and the effect measure used for synthesis (pooled rate with logit transformation)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_12_e2",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The text reports the summarized reinfection rate and confidence intervals but does not specify thresholds or ranges used to interpret the effect size (e.g., defining what constitutes a high or low rate) or provide a rationale for such thresholds."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_12_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_9",
      "quote": "Therefore, we converted the reinfection rate to an approximate normal distribution. Four transformations were taken: log transformation, logit transformation, arcsine transformation, and double arcsine transformation... we decided to use the logit transformation",
      "reason": "The text describes the method used to re-express the synthesized results (converting rate to logit transformation) to handle statistical issues."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_12_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_9",
      "quote": "However, when the rate is close to 0 or 1, two problems will occur in the meta-regression: the confidence interval may exceed the interval of 0-1, and the variance is squeezed towards 0. Therefore, we converted the reinfection rate to an approximate normal distribution... we decided to use the logit transformation",
      "reason": "The text provides a clear justification for the choice of the logit transformation (to avoid CI exceeding 0-1 and variance issues)."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 95
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_13a",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_13a_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
