      "quote": "The inclusion criteria were: (1) Conformed to research questions, i.e., studies that estimated the reinfection rate of SARS-CoV-2 or we could calculate it based on the data provided in the paper; (2) The study design included cohort study, case-control study, and descriptive study; (3) The study fited our working definition of SARS-CoV-2 reinfection... (4) Original research. The exclusion criteria were: (1) The sample size was less than 20; (2) Belonged to one of the following types of studies: editorial, case report, case series study, systematic review, meta-analysis, animal experiment, news report; (3) Secondary reporting or articles on repeated studies of the same population; (4) Grey literature... The reviewers independently (CY, Z-WH, H-XY, C-MS, LX, H-HP) screened the literature based on inclusion and exclusion criteria.",
      "reason": "The manuscript explicitly describes the inclusion and exclusion criteria used to determine study eligibility and details the independent screening process performed by reviewers. Additionally, text_8 specifies further exclusions for the meta-analysis based on data availability (e.g., unreported infection numbers) and duplicate populations."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
}

